WEBVTT

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.860
Mt. Tanigawa?

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.820
<i>The mountain I climbed with 
Hinata when we were little...</i>

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:39.370
<i>was Mt. Tanigawa.</i>

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.080
<i>That beautiful sunrise...</i>

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.860
<i>The unforgettable scenery...</i>

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:49.040
<i>I want to see them again, with Hinata.</i>

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.790
<i>Or so I thought...</i>

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.570
What? You're scared?

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.670
<i>It's just, it has a ropeway!</i>

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.480
<i>I can't handle it!</i>

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.180
Why are you saying this now?

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.140
It's just, I freak out even by thinking 
about it! That's just so high up!

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.430
<i>In that case, maybe ask 
Kaede-san for some advice?</i>

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:09.810
Beg her in your hour of need!

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:11.930
I hate to keep relying on people so much.

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.470
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.580
<i>Relying on others is a skill in itself!</i>

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.760
Says the girl who always relies on others!

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.200
<i>Huh? What did you say?</i>

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.000
Oh, nothing.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.200
Anyway, sure! I'll try texting Kaede-san.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.200
 

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.200
"Hello...

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.730
Next time I'd like to climb Mt. Tanigawa.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.460
Could you give me some advice?"

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:34.960
Send!

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.720
She already replied!

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.430
Messages

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.430
Kaede-san

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.430
Contact

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.510
"Sure, I'd be happy to!

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:45.430
But I'm meeting with someone today, 
so let's do it tomorrow, okay?"

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:47.930
Mountain Trail

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:48.930
Season 2 - New Climb 16

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.190
Season 2 - New Climb 16 
 Inheriting Sentiment

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.070
Aoi-chan!

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.460
Over here!

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.200
Aoi-san!

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:02.000
You're late!

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.340
Sorry I'm late.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.590
It's fine.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:06.650
Huh?

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:10.170
Kaede-san, what's happened to you today?

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:14.710
Well, my friend was nagging 
me to dress a bit more girly.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.410
That's me, Yuuka!

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.880
Do I look strange?

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:19.870
That's incredibly trendy!

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.630
It looks really good on you!

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:23.150
R-Really?

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.640
Yeah, just how a young lady looks!

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.610
Yes!

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.560
You look like you belong in the highlands!

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:31.180
All right, let's go back to my place.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:32.310
Okay!

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.550
That reminds me, this is our first 
time visiting Kaede-san's house.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:37.230
Yeah!

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:40.070
The home of Kaede-san, mountain girl...

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:43.070
Just what sort of house could it be?

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:46.330
Perhaps it's like Mt. Fuji?

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.160
Or like Showa-shinzan?

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:52.660
M-Maybe it's like Everest?!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.040
No, no!

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.700
Look, we're here!

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.420
Welcome!

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.680
While not what I imagined, it's very lovely!

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.600
Skylight... Roof beams...

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.770
It's like Heidi's cabin!

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:13.960
Heidi?

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.170
Of the Alps!

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.030
Who?

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.820
My room's a bit cramped, but 
please make yourselves at home.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.740
No, it's very spacious!

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.340
Here, help yourselves!

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:24.690
Thank you!

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.740
Thanks for the drinks!

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:29.400
It's so good!

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.350
Yeah, what with the heat today.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.640
Kaede-san, how did your climb go, 
at that one mountain ridge?

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.040
In the Northern Alps?

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.050
Oh, that place.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.300
It's called the Big Gap.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:42.700
Gap?

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:46.160
It's where a mountain has been eroded 
through to form a low-lying area.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.430
The Japanese word can be 
either "<i>kiretto</i>" or "<i>kireto</i>".

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.550
In kanji characters, 
it's written as "Cut Place",

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:53.930
or as "Cut Door".

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.280
You really know a lot, Kokona-chan!

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:57.190
Check it out!

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.020
I'd always wanted to visit this place!

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.110
It's so pretty!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.350
It is, it is!

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.120
It's <i>crazy</i> pretty!

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.560
And thrilling, too!

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.370
With lots of amazing trails!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.290
Like this one!

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.240
Wow!

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.710
It's on the edge of a cliff!

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:20.460
Some spots have scaffolding like this in place,

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:24.320
but there's a sheer hundred-meter drop beneath!

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:25.720
Oh no!

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:29.400
W-Would you die if you fell there?

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.440
Oh yes! Most definitely!

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.160
What an amazing climb!

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.140
Impressive as always, Kaede-san!

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.300
Um, Kaede-san?

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.880
I've been wondering this for a while, but...

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.810
how is it that you can handle such scary places?

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:46.780
I mean...

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:51.970
I was really wanting to go climb Mt. Tanigawa,

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:53.910
but it has a ropeway.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:56.240
I just know I'll get too scared.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.920
Yeah, with your fear of heights.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:01.450
But, I still really want to go!

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:05.880
Kaede-san, you've said that you 
used to be afraid of heights too.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.930
So I was hoping you could 
tell me how you overcame it.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.820
Yes, I see.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.680
Ropeways can be pretty scary.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:15.680
When I first started out,

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:19.890
I got freaked out by the jolt it made 
when passing over those support posts.

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:21.540
<i>We are approaching a support post.</i>

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.490
<i>Beware of shaking.</i>

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:30.410
I freaked out and clung tightly to the pole, 
afraid that the floor was about to give way.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.720
Why are you freaking out now?

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.240
It's just, I can't help imagining it!

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:37.600
But you know,

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.030
after riding it a few times,

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.650
I was so used to it that I didn't feel a thing.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:43.390
After a few times?

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:44.270
Right.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:48.220
It's like, whatever frightens you feels 
like nothing, once you're used to it...

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:53.990
Or maybe, being convinced that you'll 
be scared is what makes you anxious,

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:56.970
even when it's really no big deal...

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.410
No big deal...

00:06:59.410 --> 00:06:59.980
Right!

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:01.870
For example, when mountain climbing,

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:05.970
a part that was scary on the climb up 
isn't very scary on the way back down.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.730
Haven't you had that experience?

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.240
<i>At Mt. Mitsutouge,</i>

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:16.270
<i>I didn't feel very scared at 
that cliff on the way back down.</i>

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:22.290
Your own heart, telling you you're anxious, 
could be making you afraid for no good reason.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.600
My own... heart...

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.420
You should declare, "This is where I'm going!"

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:33.600
Then you'll have no choice but to go.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:36.290
I think you'll be able to 
prepare yourself with that.

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:39.930
You can always turn back at 
any time if it gets dangerous.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.460
If you're uncertain, why not 
move forward for the time being?

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:45.690
The answer will come along eventually!

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:53.240
<i>Once I start walking, 
there may be nothing to it.</i>

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.120
Aoi!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.200
Aoi-san!

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:56.930
<i>That's right...</i>

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.370
<i>I'll keep going,</i>

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:01.980
<i>stepping forward with all my might!</i>

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.200
Th-Then...

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.700
Hinata, Kokona-chan, Kaede-san...

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:12.340
would you come with me to visit 
 Mt.Tanigawa during summer break?!

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:14.870
Sure! Fine by me!

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.110
Of course I'm okay with it!

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:17.220
I am as well!

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:19.720
Thank you!

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:22.140
At last, Mt. Tanigawa...

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.440
It took a long ways getting here.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.230
By the way, why Mt. Tanigawa?

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:31.030
Partly because you recommended 
it earlier, Kaede-san,

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.570
but also...

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:36.590
because I climbed it before 
as a kid, with Hinata.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:37.590
That's right!

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:39.360
It's Mt. Tanigawa of our memories!

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.100
You say that smugly,

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:44.300
but you didn't even remember 
which mountain it was!

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.500
Neither did you!

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:47.540
It was during grade school.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:51.000
Before I became afraid of heights,

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:55.780
I made a memory of a truly beautiful sunrise,

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.510
that I want to see again.

00:08:57.860 --> 00:08:59.030
I see!

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:01.150
For that, we'll spend the night in a hut!

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:04.020
Oh, that's right! I'd better make reservations!

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:07.830
Well, whether or not we see 
the sunrise is a matter of luck...

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.610
Tends to attract rain...

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:11.740
I do hope it will be sunny.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:12.740
Yeah!

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.540
This talk of weather reminds me.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:17.990
I want to check that everybody has the proper 
equipment, like with our Mt. Fuji trip.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.620
Do you all have raincoats?

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:20.740
Raincoats?

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.990
I've got one!

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.340
I bought a bit of an expensive one with 
the savings from my recent part-time job!

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:26.670
Isn't that great?

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:28.920
Now I kinda hope it rains!

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:32.420
But if it rains, you won't 
be able to see the sunrise.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:33.890
Oh, right!

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:34.800
Silly!

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.620
I'm fine as well.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:40.680
It's a little old, but I have the 
raincoat that Mom used to use.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:41.790
I see.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:42.810
And you, Aoi-chan?

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:44.810
I... don't have one.

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:49.190
I've been thinking that I should buy 
a raincoat, but then I looked into it...

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.860
They're pretty expensive.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.020
Aoi-chan, how tall are you?

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.870
Uh, 152 centimeters.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.230
Wait just a minute!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:10.080
Say, could you use my old one?

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:13.050
I bought it back in middle school,

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:14.230
but I can't wear it anymore,

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:15.870
so I'll give it to you, Aoi-chan!

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.990
A-Are you sure?!

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.720
I've been wondering what to do with it.

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:22.500
Since I picked it out with my friend,

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.470
I didn't want to just get rid of it!

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:27.480
I'd be very happy if you could use it, Aoi-chan!

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:30.200
Thank you very much!

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:34.420
Lucky you!

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.190
Isn't that great, Aoi-san?

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.190
Yeah!

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.310
Aoi-chan, would you try it on for me real quick?

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:42.950
Sure!

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.960
H-How do I look?

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.460
It suits you really well!

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:52.770
It's great!

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:53.670
Perfect!

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.740
Sorry that it's a bit beat up.

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:59.590
It's fine, I love it!

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:01.180
Thank you very much!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.900
I'll put all my might into the trip planning!

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:05.370
Sure! You can do it!

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:06.220
Thanks!

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.620
Yes, you can do it!

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:08.490
Sure!

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:09.500
You can do it!

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:10.440
Oh, shut up!

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.390
Hey, why do <i>I</i> get that reaction?!

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:14.430
Like you have to ask!

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.690
But I'm cheering you on like I should!

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.210
Just shut up!

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:32.080
I'd better plan this well, or 
else Hinata will laugh at me!

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.420
Monthly Famous Mountain Guide - Mt. Tanigawa

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:45.470
Getting to Tenjin Plain and the lifts 
takes about 7 minutes by ropeway.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:46.900
From there...

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:48.490
<i>I have to screw up my courage,</i>

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:50.140
<i>and take a step forward!</i>

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:51.980
<i>Because up ahead,</i>

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:55.880
<i>there's sure to be lovely 
scenery waiting for me!</i>

00:11:57.560 --> 00:11:59.980
To Be Continued!
